{
  "$schema": "./SCHEMA.md#device-grant-approval",
  "description": "Device grant approval signing bytes (avalon_protocol::identity_id::device_grant_approval_signing_bytes): tag avalon.device_grant.approved, version 1, fields grant_id (uuid), identity_id (32 raw bytes), approver_signing_key_id (uuid), requested device public key (32 raw bytes), seq (u64), prev_hash (flag byte, then 32 bytes when present). The approver signs the chain position the approval will occupy: seq is the identity chain head seq plus one and prev_hash the head event hash, absent for the first chained event. The grant id is also the id of the key the grant creates. The layout is the structured signing-bytes encoding (avalon_protocol::signing_bytes): the ASCII domain tag with no length, a u16 big-endian version (1), then the fields in the order listed. str is a u32 big-endian byte length and the UTF-8 bytes; uuid is its 16 raw bytes; identity ids and public keys are 32 raw bytes; seq is a u64 big-endian; prev_hash is one byte (0 = no previous event, 1 = a 32-byte event hash follows). The signature is Ed25519 by the signer key over the bytes, verified strictly. replayVectors offer a signature made for one input with another input's bytes; legacyLayoutVectors carry a signature over the retired text layout. Neither may verify.",
  "generation": "Generated by scripts/gen-identity-key-event-vectors.py, an encoder that shares no code with the Rust one (cryptography Ed25519, hashlib). signingKeySeedHex is the Ed25519 seed of the signer; Ed25519 signatures are deterministic.",
